From b372d6c75d9e4276b2635d5d24ced80e2ac541d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:57:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Tormach lifts Z after each tool change before
 moving X/Y

Every Tormach mill tool change posted G53 G0 Z0, G30, T.. M6, G43 H..,
the spindle, then G0 X Y with no Z lift between. A bare G30 leaves Z at
the stored G30 height; one stored below the part top (the user's
PathPilot Hub sim had machine Z -1.5611, the cause of #1594) rapids the
tool sideways at that height into the part or the vise.

startPreamble now writes liftZ() (G53 G0 Z0, or the machine's stated
safe Z, #495) right after the G43 line, before the spindle start and the
section's first X/Y or A move. The tool-change G30 stays (PathPilot's
convention). The plasma and lathe G30s are kept with the reasons in
docs/decisions/1596-toolchange-lift.md; the lathe's diagonal approach
from G30 is filed as #1604.

Pinned by tormach_toolchange_lift (every shipped Tormach mill, a stated
safe Z, the 4th-axis A index); tormach_safe_retract and
probe_spindle_stop updated. 33 NC goldens gain only G53 G0 Z0 lines (35).

Fixes #1596

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
